          "claim": "The refs_changed (field=freshness) event is asserted to embed the branch OID and literal \"null\" (assertIn(oids[name], json.dumps(event)) / json.dumps(freshness[0])). The monitor contract enumerates event fields as id,route,consumer,condition,monitor,subject,state,summary,evidence-reference,observed_at,delivery with summary from the named metric (the freshness word) and evidence={repo,remote,ref}; OIDs live in metrics {local_oid,remote_oid,freshness} which the event references, not inlines. A contract-correct reader whose refs_changed event carries summary=freshness word and evidence={repo,remote,ref} contains no OID and is wrongly rejected. The aggregate json.dumps(events) assertions survive via the separate local_changed/remote_changed events; only the per-freshness-event OID/null embedding is unsupported.",
